---
name: use-highlighted-code
type: registry:hook
title: Use Highlighted Code
description: Reactive Shiki token lines for code blocks, including incremental updates.
dependencies:
  - shiki
files:
  - path: registry/items/utilities/use-highlighted-code/use-highlighted-code.svelte.ts
    type: registry:hook
    target: "~/hooks/use-highlighted-code.svelte.ts"
  - path: registry/items/utilities/use-highlighted-code/highlighter.ts
    type: registry:hook
    target: "~/hooks/highlighter.ts"
---

Call during component initialization and pass getters for reactive source and language values. `current` returns plain text while the highlighter loads, then styled token arrays accepted by `CodeBlock.Line`. Unsupported languages remain plain text. Install [Code Block](/components/code-block) separately for the example below.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { useHighlightedCode } from "~/hooks/use-highlighted-code.svelte.js";
  import * as CodeBlock from "~/components/code-block";
  let code = $state('const greeting = "hello";');
  const lines = useHighlightedCode(() => code, () => "typescript");
</script>

<CodeBlock.Root>
  <CodeBlock.Content lineNumbers>
    {#each lines.current as line, index (index)}
      <CodeBlock.Line code={line} />
    {/each}
  </CodeBlock.Content>
</CodeBlock.Root>
```

Includes lazy language loading, GitHub light and dark token colors, ANSI, and common language aliases such as `ts`, `js`, and `sh`. Extend `highlighter.ts` to enable additional languages.
